# Copy to server/.env. With nothing set the server runs in local mode
# (embedded database in .data/, passwords checked by the API).

# --- Database: PostgreSQL (production) ---
# Set this to use a real PostgreSQL 15+ instead of the embedded one.
# Local install:  postgres://hrm_app:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/hrm
# Hosted (Neon, Supabase, Render, RDS...) usually needs ?sslmode=require at the end.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://hrm_app:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/hrm

# --- Firebase Authentication (optional) ---
# Service account key: Firebase console > Project settings > Service accounts >
# Generate new private key. Save the file next to this one; never commit it.
# With DATABASE_URL set, Firebase is used for sign-in only and the data stays
# in PostgreSQL (recommended). Without DATABASE_URL, FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL also
# makes Realtime Database the system of record (single API instance only).
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=./firebase-service-account.json
# FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://hrm-techexa-a6e1b-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com
# FIREBASE_DB_ROOT=hrm

# --- Email (Resend) ---
# Takes priority over SMTP. Key from resend.com > API Keys; RESEND_FROM must be on a domain verified in Resend
# (until then only onboarding@resend.dev, delivering only to your Resend account email).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxx
# RESEND_FROM="HRM <no-reply@yourcompany.com>"

# --- Email (SMTP) ---
# Without SMTP_HOST, emails are only written to the server log.
# Check the settings with:  npm run email:test -- you@example.com
#   Gmail:    smtp.gmail.com, port 587, your address + an App Password
#             (Google account > Security > 2-Step Verification > App passwords)
#   Outlook:  smtp.office365.com, port 587
#   Zoho:     smtp.zoho.com, port 587
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false            # true for port 465
# SMTP_USER=hr@yourcompany.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-app-password
# SMTP_FROM="HRM <hr@yourcompany.com>"

# --- Online card payments (Stripe Checkout) ---
# Without these, companies pay by bank transfer and the super admin records it.
# Keys: dashboard.stripe.com > Developers > API keys (use sk_test_... while testing).
# Webhook: Developers > Webhooks > Add endpoint  https://YOUR-API/api/billing/webhook
#   events: checkout.session.completed, checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded, checkout.session.expired
#   then copy its "Signing secret" (whsec_...). Locally: `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:4000/api/billing/webhook`
#   prints a whsec_ to use here.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# --- Web app address ---
# Used in sign-up confirmation links and to send people back after paying.
# APP_URL=http://localhost:5300

# --- General ---
# JWT_SECRET=change-me        # required in production (long random string)
# PORT=4000
# JOBS_INTERVAL_S=300         # background jobs (auto-close, escalation, email)
